{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/layoutsystem"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit uses a two-pass layout system inspired by SwiftUI’s layout protocol. Layout containers like "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack"},{"type":"text","text":" first "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"measure"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" each child, then "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"render"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" them with allocated sizes. This approach enables features like flexible spacers, proportional sizing, and proper alignment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Two-Passes","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Two Passes"},{"anchor":"Pass-1-Measure","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Pass 1: Measure"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The parent proposes a size to each child via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ProposedSize"},{"type":"text","text":". Each child responds with a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ViewSize"},{"type":"text","text":" that describes how much space it needs and whether it can flex."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Parent (VStack)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Text    → ViewSize(10, 1, flexible: false)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Spacer  → ViewSize(0, 0, flexible: true)","  └─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Button  → ViewSize(12, 1, flexible: false)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"anchor":"Pass-2-Render","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Pass 2: Render"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After measuring all children, the parent distributes the remaining space among flexible children and renders each child with its final allocated size.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Parent allocates:","  Text   → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height","  Spacer → render(width: 40, height: 8)   \/\/ Gets remaining vertical space","  Button → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"anchor":"ProposedSize","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"ProposedSize"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ProposedSize"},{"text":" represents the space a parent offers to a child. Either dimension can be ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", meaning “use your ideal size.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public struct ProposedSize {","    public var width: Int?","    public var height: Int?","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Meaning","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use ideal size (no constraint)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Minimum size","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"> 0","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Available space in characters\/lines"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"anchor":"ViewSize","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"ViewSize"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ViewSize","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the child’s response: how much space it needs and whether it can expand."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public struct ViewSize {","    public var width: Int","    public var height: Int","    public var isWidthFlexible: Bool","    public var isHeightFlexible: Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Factory methods make common patterns concise:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ViewSize.fixed(20, 1)                    \/\/ Fixed 20x1, won't expand","ViewSize.flexible(minWidth: 0, minHeight: 0)  \/\/ Expands in both directions","ViewSize.flexibleWidth(minWidth: 5, height: 1) \/\/ Expands horizontally only"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"The-Layoutable-Protocol","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Layoutable Protocol"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Views that participate in two-pass layout conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Layoutable"},{"type":"text","text":" (which extends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Renderable"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["protocol Layoutable: Renderable {","    func sizeThatFits(proposal: ProposedSize, context: RenderContext) -> ViewSize","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A default implementation renders the view and measures the resulting buffer. Custom implementations can calculate size without rendering for better performance."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"ChildView","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"ChildView"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Layout containers wrap their children in ","type":"text"},{"code":"ChildView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which provides a uniform interface for measuring and rendering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ChildView {","    func measure(proposal: ProposedSize, context: RenderContext) -> ViewSize","    func render(width: Int, height: Int, context: RenderContext) -> FrameBuffer","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ChildView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically detects spacers and propagates child identity for correct state management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"How-Stacks-Lay-Out-Children","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"How Stacks Lay Out Children"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" follow this algorithm:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measure"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" all children with the parent’s proposed size","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sum"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the fixed sizes along the stack axis","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Distribute"}]},{"type":"text","text":" remaining space among flexible children (spacers, flexible text fields, etc.)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Render","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" each child with its allocated size","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compose"}]},{"text":" the rendered buffers with the specified spacing and alignment","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flexible children share remaining space equally. If multiple spacers exist, they each get an equal portion of the leftover space."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Which-Views-Are-Layoutable","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Which Views Are Layoutable?"},{"rows":[